## Why This Is Asked

Tests a candidate's ability to design a compliant, language-agnostic text classification pipeline using Vertex AI, Dataflow, and Pub/Sub, with privacy safeguards and practical operational concerns.

## Key Concepts

- Dataflow-based redaction and translation for multilingual content
- End-to-end data lineage: storage of raw and processed text
- Weekly Vertex AI training with canary deployment
- Drift and latency monitoring with rollback strategy
- Practical cost considerations: storage, translation, training, and serving

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: dataflow-style transform for redaction/translation
function redactAndTranslate(record) {
  const redacted = redactPII(record.text);
  const translated = (record.language !== 'en') ? translate(redacted, 'en') : redacted;
  return { id: record.id, text_en: translated, raw: record.text };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate translation quality across languages in this setup?
- What changes would you make to handle sudden traffic spikes without violating privacy constraints?

## Why This Is Asked
This probes ability to design privacy-aware, geo-distributed ML pipelines on GCP, balancing data residency, DP, drift and cost.

## Key Concepts
- Vertex AI training/serving (region-scoped)
- Vertex AI Feature Store (per-region stores)
- Dataflow for streaming ETL with DP transforms
- Pub/Sub for event ingestion
- Differential privacy, drift detection, automatic rollback, cost caps

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo DP transform sketch
function dpClipAndNoise(features, clipBound, epsilon) {
  Object.keys(features).forEach(k => {
    features[k] = Math.max(-clipBound, Math.min(clipBound, features[k]));
  });
  for (let k in features) { features[k] += laplace(1/epsilon); }
  return features;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-region data residency for training data across regions?
- How would you test canary rollouts and rollback safety at scale?
- How would you monitor DP utility vs. model accuracy in production?
